                          <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>Bucket Description </run>
                          <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                          <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                          <run fontcolor='#d3293d' fontname='Tableau Bold'>1.Product Shared &amp; Not Listed at vendor- To be assigned to Vendor: </run>
                          <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Bold'> Products Listed in Catalog Chain Level or Barcode are listed in PIM  but not assigned to vendor. These SKU/Barcode are being shared via SFTP </run>
                          <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                          <run fontcolor='#d3293d' fontname='Tableau Bold'>2.Product Shared &amp; Not Available- New Content Creation: </run>
                          <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Bold'>Products are NOT available in Catalog or PIM. These SKU/barcode are being shared via SFTP</run>
                          <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                          <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d3293d' fontname='Tableau Bold'>3.Product Shared &amp; Available - Already Assigned:</run>
                          <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ae0318' fontname='Tableau Bold'>Æ </run>
                          <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Bold'>Products Available in Catalog and PIM and Updates are being shared by Vendors via SFTP </run>
                          <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                          <run fontcolor='#d3293d' fontname='Tableau Bold'>4.Products Not shared &amp; Available: </run>
                          <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Bold'>Æ </run>
                          <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Bold'>Product are available in Catalog and PIM but are not being shared by the vendor via SFTP</run>
                          <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                          <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                          <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Bold'>NOTE: Chain Level Counts are at chain_name x geid level (similar to chain product id level in catalog) &amp; Vendor Level Counts are at vendor x geid level (similar to vendor product id level in catalog). A product will be either SKU or barcode (if SKU is not shared )</run>
